  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In the 1990s, the story goes, NASA announced it had found signs of an unknown extra planet, a \"Planet 10\". Then a scientist named Myles Standish redid the maths and concluded, in effect, \"we made a mistake\", and the planet was dropped. The researcher Matt LaCroix tells Michels this from memory, without naming a source, and offers it as a case where a possible new world was announced and then quietly taken back."
